- On this episode, I'm gonna find out

00:00:01.904 --> 00:00:04.992
if you have the goods, the chops, the it.

00:00:04.992 --> 00:00:07.523
Redhead quarterbacks, and finally,

00:00:07.523 --> 00:00:09.918
me forgetting something.

00:00:09.918 --> 00:00:14.918
(heavy bass hip-hop beat)

00:00:19.643 --> 00:00:22.638
What's up everybody?
This is Gary Vaynerchuk,

00:00:22.638 --> 00:00:26.307
and this is #AskGaryVee, Episode 6.

00:00:26.307 --> 00:00:28.838
- [Voiceover] Jason asks,
"What's the best way

00:00:28.838 --> 00:00:30.858
"to use Facebook dark posts?"

00:00:30.858 --> 00:00:32.530
- Jason, what's up man?
This is a great question

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:35.339
to start Episode 6 with
because it's a general question

00:00:35.339 --> 00:00:37.081
that I want everybody to pay attention to.

00:00:37.081 --> 00:00:39.031
Jason's asking about Facebook dark posts,

00:00:39.031 --> 00:00:40.935
you might be thinking about
how to make Instagram work,

00:00:40.935 --> 00:00:44.975
or the up-and-coming amazing
Pinterest CPC ad platform,

00:00:44.975 --> 00:00:46.693
or anything, native ads on Outbrain

00:00:46.693 --> 00:00:48.435
and Taboola and Hexagram.

00:00:48.435 --> 00:00:52.034
The real answer to this, Jason,
is to become a practitioner.

00:00:52.034 --> 00:00:55.470
The right price for your ads
is always a moving variable

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:59.046
based on supply and demand,
competition, all that jazz.

00:00:59.046 --> 00:01:01.995
The way to become good at it is to do it.

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:05.617
You can go, step one, go
to YouTube and Google,

00:01:05.617 --> 00:01:07.358
and look up all the information,

00:01:07.358 --> 00:01:10.377
and figure out how to become
better at Facebook dark posts,

00:01:10.377 --> 00:01:13.418
read 30 articles on AllFacebook.com about

00:01:13.418 --> 00:01:16.089
how to be better at Facebook dark posts.

00:01:16.089 --> 00:01:18.852
You can do all the homework,
but until you apply it,

00:01:18.852 --> 00:01:20.570
it's just knowledge, isn't it?

00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:22.915
And I love students, but only so much.

00:01:22.915 --> 00:01:25.306
And so, the answer to
your question, my friend,

00:01:25.306 --> 00:01:27.977
is very simple: become
educated and execute.

00:01:27.977 --> 00:01:30.229
That's how everything works,
for every single answer,

00:01:30.229 --> 00:01:31.761
on all these issues.

00:01:31.761 --> 00:01:34.362
To find out the right price,
there is no right price, Jason,

00:01:34.362 --> 00:01:37.125
the right price is the right
price right this second,

00:01:37.125 --> 00:01:38.936
because of the supply and demand curve

00:01:38.936 --> 00:01:40.585
of what you're trying to apply.

00:01:40.585 --> 00:01:41.885
If you're trying to sell furniture,

00:01:41.885 --> 00:01:43.487
and you're one of two people buying ads

00:01:43.487 --> 00:01:45.066
on Facebook dark posts for furniture,

00:01:45.066 --> 00:01:47.225
your cost is gonna be a better
deal than in three weeks,

00:01:47.225 --> 00:01:49.594
when five people are there
trying to bid that up.

00:01:49.594 --> 00:01:51.497
Supply and demand, supply and demand.

00:01:51.497 --> 00:01:54.191
- [Voiceover] Dawn asks, "Do
you feel it's still a necessary

00:01:54.191 --> 00:01:57.256
"call to action to push
subscribers from social channels

00:01:57.256 --> 00:01:59.833
"to a website or newsletter sign-up?"

00:01:59.833 --> 00:02:02.341
- Dawn, who says I ever thought it was

00:02:02.341 --> 00:02:04.314
a necessary call to action,
'cause the answer is

00:02:04.314 --> 00:02:06.311
I didn't, and I don't.

00:02:06.311 --> 00:02:08.656
No I don't. No I didn't.

00:02:08.656 --> 00:02:11.744
What I mean by that is, sure,
I think it's a good idea

00:02:11.744 --> 00:02:13.556
to push to a website right now,

00:02:13.556 --> 00:02:16.040
especially if you're selling
something on that website.

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:18.432
But in a world where you
can buy that same product

00:02:18.432 --> 00:02:21.195
right on Twitter, right on Facebook,

00:02:21.195 --> 00:02:23.749
do you necessarily need to
schlep somebody to your site

00:02:23.749 --> 00:02:26.396
to make them buy that, when
it's native right for them,

00:02:26.396 --> 00:02:27.951
and they could just buy it in there?

00:02:27.951 --> 00:02:29.368
No, the answer is no, isn't it?

00:02:29.368 --> 00:02:31.179
'Cause friction sucks, right?

00:02:31.179 --> 00:02:34.128
Friction sucks, and consumers
do not want friction,

00:02:34.128 --> 00:02:35.939
so anything that allows you to execute

00:02:35.939 --> 00:02:38.934
within the place you're in,
that's what you're gonna like.

00:02:38.934 --> 00:02:41.209
And so, my answer to your question is,

00:02:41.209 --> 00:02:42.765
less and less every day.

00:02:42.765 --> 00:02:44.437
People always say, Gary, why
aren't you driving people

00:02:44.437 --> 00:02:46.573
to GaryVaynerchuk.com?

00:02:46.573 --> 00:02:48.686
Why are you putting
out content on YouTube?

00:02:48.686 --> 00:02:50.311
Why are you putting out content on Medium?

00:02:50.311 --> 00:02:51.867
Why are you putting content on LinkedIn?

00:02:51.867 --> 00:02:53.748
Because I want awareness,
so I'm putting out content

00:02:53.748 --> 00:02:57.230
for awareness and to build
relationships with all of you.

00:02:57.230 --> 00:02:59.529
That's what I'm doing, and thus,

00:02:59.529 --> 00:03:01.712
what that is doing is creating a scenario

00:03:01.712 --> 00:03:04.173
where those channels allow me to do that.

00:03:04.173 --> 00:03:06.100
Just because I'm not
driving them to my dot--

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:08.770
You know how many people give
you bad marketing advice?

00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:11.533
That say, "You have to
drive to your website."

00:03:11.533 --> 00:03:13.739
For what? To collect the email?

00:03:13.739 --> 00:03:17.083
Last time I checked, a tweet
card that collects email

00:03:17.083 --> 00:03:19.405
has been the most efficient
way that I've collected email,

00:03:19.405 --> 00:03:21.216
better than driving to my dot com.

00:03:21.216 --> 00:03:23.956
For what? What are you, selling
advertising on your site?

00:03:23.956 --> 00:03:25.767
If you're selling
advertising on your site,

00:03:25.767 --> 00:03:27.299
then maybe that's the thing you could do,

00:03:27.299 --> 00:03:29.087
but you can also sell advertising

00:03:29.087 --> 00:03:30.828
to people within your social channels

00:03:30.828 --> 00:03:32.082
and run that arbitrage.

00:03:32.082 --> 00:03:33.568
So the fact of the matter is, Dawn,

00:03:33.568 --> 00:03:36.810
is that I think people are
just not really that educated

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:38.412
on what they're trying to achieve.

00:03:38.412 --> 00:03:40.943
And so I've never been
worried about forcing somebody

00:03:40.943 --> 00:03:43.614
to a dot com, unless that
was the right strategy

00:03:43.614 --> 00:03:46.005
at the right time to drive the result.

00:03:46.005 --> 00:03:48.002
The fact that even e-commerce,

00:03:48.002 --> 00:03:50.115
buying within a tweet and a Facebook post,

00:03:50.115 --> 00:03:52.994
has now gotten native the platform,

00:03:52.994 --> 00:03:54.759
has eliminated a lot of the reasons

00:03:54.759 --> 00:03:57.266
that you have to drive somebody.

00:03:57.266 --> 00:03:58.915
- [Voiceover] Nam asks, "How did you deal

00:03:58.915 --> 00:04:01.028
"with working in a family business?"

00:04:01.028 --> 00:04:03.652
- Nam, very carefully.

00:04:03.652 --> 00:04:05.834
Family businesses are difficult.

00:04:05.834 --> 00:04:10.581
I'm in my second one, my dad, my brother.

00:04:10.581 --> 00:04:12.973
I look forward to my one
with my kids one day.

00:04:12.973 --> 00:04:15.527
Misha and Xander, if you wanna
be an entrepreneur, call me.

00:04:15.527 --> 00:04:18.360
Um, you know,

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:20.007
I think the real answer is, Nam,

00:04:20.007 --> 00:04:22.144
the reason I've had two
successful family businesses,

00:04:22.144 --> 00:04:25.604
is very simply, and kudos to my dad,

00:04:25.604 --> 00:04:27.996
and kudos to my mom, and kudos to just,

00:04:27.996 --> 00:04:30.875
a lot of fortunate things
that allowed my dad and I,

00:04:30.875 --> 00:04:33.382
and now my brother and
I, to allow our love

00:04:33.382 --> 00:04:37.562
to trump our pride, our competitiveness,

00:04:37.562 --> 00:04:40.069
our business POVs,

00:04:40.069 --> 00:04:42.925
somehow in our specific situation,

00:04:42.925 --> 00:04:44.876
probably predicated
with a lot of hard work,

00:04:44.876 --> 00:04:47.755
specifically from my mom,
more than you would think,

00:04:47.755 --> 00:04:50.007
and my dad, and then the incredible

00:04:50.007 --> 00:04:52.631
natural DNA that they gifted me,

00:04:52.631 --> 00:04:54.930
we have created a situation
where we've allowed,

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:57.159
at the end of the day,
for us not to lose focus

00:04:57.159 --> 00:04:59.388
on the fact that we love each other

00:04:59.388 --> 00:05:02.151
more than we care about getting our way.

